 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "Rules are deferred while the bundle is defined and applied to the app at registration time.\n\n1. **Deferral:** `Bundle.attach_route_rule` (`src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py:413`) is also what `@bundle.route` goes through, via `Scaffold.route` in `src/tessel/sansio/scaffold.py:344`. It doesn't touch the app. It calls `Bundle.record(...)` (`bundles.py:224`) with a lambda that calls `state.attach_route_rule(...)`, and `record` appends that lambda to `self.deferred_functions`.\n\n2. **Registration entry point:** `Tessel.register_bundle` (`src/tessel/sansio/app.py:571`) calls `bundle.register(self, options)` (`app.py:596`).\n\n3. **Replay:** `Bundle.register` (`bundles.py:273`) does the following:\n   - Builds a `BundleSetupState` through `make_setup_state` (`bundles.py:246`). The state resolves `url_prefix`, `subdomain`, `name_prefix` and `url_defaults`.\n   - Runs `for deferred in self.deferred_functions: deferred(state)` (`bundles.py:334`).\n   - Registers the static route itself when the bundle has a static folder (`bundles.py:324`).\n   - Recurses into nested bundles with the combined prefix and subdomain (`bundles.py:349`).\n\n4. **Applying the rule:** `BundleSetupState.attach_route_rule` (`bundles.py:87`) does the following:\n   - Prepends `url_prefix` to the rule.\n   - Sets the subdomain and merges the URL defaults.\n   - Prefixes the endpoint name as `name_prefix.name.endpoint`.\n   - Calls `app.attach_route_rule(...)` (`src/tessel/sansio/app.py:606`), which adds the rule to the app's URL map.",
